  * Topic\nL153: \nL154: [Input] About arXivLabs\nL155: # arXivLabs: experimental projects with community collaborators\nL156: \nL157: arXivLabs is a framework that allows collaborators to develop and share new arXiv features directly on our website.\nL158: \nL159: Both individuals and organizations that work with arXivLabs have embraced and accepted our values of openness, community, excellence, and user data privacy. arXiv is committed to these values and only works with partners that adhere to them.\nL160: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? cite47†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org .\nL161: \nL162: cite48†Which authors of this paper are endorsers? | Disable MathJax (cite49†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org )\nL163: \nL164: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite50†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL165: cite51†About†info.arxiv.org · cite52†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite53†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite54†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite55†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite56†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite57†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite58†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L166: \nL167: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2609.30057] KREX: Concurrent Kernel Benchmarking on Shared GPUs via Region-Granular Exclusivity (https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30057)\nciteturn34view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30057\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 164\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 24 Sep 2026]\nL9: # Title:KREX: Concurrent Kernel Benchmarking on Shared GPUs via Region-Granular Exclusivity\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Tianyu Feng , cite6†Haoxuan Yu , cite7†Tianyuan Wu , cite8†Lingyun Yang , cite9†Daocheng Ying , cite10†Yuxiao Wang , cite11†Ruibo Fan , cite12†Yinghao Yu , cite13†Guodong Yang , cite14†Liping Zhang , cite15†Wei Wang L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled KREX: Concurrent Kernel Benchmarking on Shared GPUs via Region-Granular Exclusivity, by Tianyu Feng and 10 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite16†View PDF cite17†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:LLM agents automate GPU kernel optimization by repeatedly composing candidates and measuring their duration on real GPUs. Existing systems preserve measurement fidelity by reserving a GPU for an entire agent session or benchmarking command. However, this results in poor utilization because only a small fraction of command execution requires exclusive GPU access.\nL17: Sharing GPUs could recover this idle capacity, but introduces contention that compromises measurement fidelity and misdirects the agent's search.\nL18: > We present KREX, a runtime for concurrent kernel agent benchmarking with region-granular exclusivity. KREX lets agents mark critical regions involving timing-sensitive operations within a benchmarking command. The runtime then enforces exclusivity within marked regions and allows concurrent execution outside them, achieving high throughput while preserving measurement fidelity.\nL19: To enforce in-region exclusivity, KREX blocks new competing GPU submissions and drains outstanding work before freezing sibling processes and isolating CPU cores, protecting both GPU execution and the host threads that drive measurements. To maximize off-region concurrency, KREX reuses GPU contexts in persistent context processes to avoid repeated, node-wide serialized context creation. We evaluate KREX on NVIDIA and AMD GPUs.\nL20: Compared with command-granular exclusivity baselines, KREX delivers up to $3.4\\times$ the benchmarking throughput with a negligible p95 timing inflation of $0.30\\%$, $1.58\\%$, and $3.90\\%$ for kernels longer than 10 ms, 1 ms, and 0.1 ms, respectively.\nL21: Comments:  | 14 pages, 12 figures\nL22: Subjects:  | Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing (cs.DC); Operating Systems (cs.OS); Performance (cs.PF)\nL23: Cite as:  | cite18†arXiv:2609.30057 [cs.DC]\nL24:    | (or cite19†arXiv:2609.30057v1 [cs.DC] for this version)\nL25:    | cite20†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2609.30057†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration)\nL26: ## Submission history\nL27: \nL28: From: Tianyu Feng [cite21†view email ]\nL29: [v1] Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:14:04 UTC (1,160 KB)\nL30: \nL31: Full-text links:\nL32: \nL33: ## Access Paper:\nL34: \nL35: View a PDF of the paper titled KREX: Concurrent Kernel Benchmarking on Shared GPUs via Region-Granular Exclusivity, by Tianyu Feng and 10 other authors\nL36: \nL37:   * cite16†View PDF L38:   * cite17†HTML (experimental) L39:   * cite22†TeX Source L40: \nL41: cite23†view license L42: ### Current browse context:\nL43: \nL44: cs.DC\nL45: \nL46: cite24†< prev |   cite25†next > L47: \nL48: cite26†new | cite27†recent | cite28†2026-09 L49: \nL50: Change to browse by:\nL51: \nL52: cite29†cs L53: cite30†cs.OS L54: cite31†cs.PF L55: \nL56: ### References & Citations\nL57: \nL58:   * cite32†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L59:   * cite33†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L60:   * cite34†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L61: \nL62: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL63: \nL64: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL65: \nL66: [Button: ×]\nL67: \nL68: loading...\nL69: \nL70: Data provided by:\nL71: \nL72: ### Bookmark\nL73: \nL74: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL75: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL76: \nL77: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL78: \nL79: Bibliographic Explore